<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>BTA Admin GPS Spoofing</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css" />
  </head>
  <body class="workspace-page">
    <main class="workspace-shell">
      <section class="hero-band">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">Integrity Scenario</p>
          <h1>GPS Spoofing Injection</h1>
          <p class="subtitle">
            Arm a spoofed bus profile here, then trigger the evidence from the customer fleet page
            so the visible bus data and Graylog events line up.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <nav class="page-nav">
            <a class="nav-link" href="/admin/dashboard">Admin Dashboard</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="/admin/passenger/tickets">Fetch Tickets</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="/admin/simulations/auth-sequence">Auth Sequence</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="/admin/simulations/dns-tunneling">DNS Tunneling</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="/admin/simulations/payment-skimming">Payment Skimming</a>
            <a class="nav-link active" href="/admin/simulations/gps-spoofing">GPS Spoofing</a>
            <a class="nav-link" href="/admin/simulations/ransomware">Ransomware</a>
          </nav>
          <form method="post" action="/logout">
            <button class="secondary" type="submit">Log Out</button>
          </form>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="detail-layout">
        <article class="detail-card detail-card-wide">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">Spoofing Profile</p>
            <span class="status-pill neutral">POST /api/simulations/gps-spoofing</span>
          </div>
          <h2>Ghost Bus Generator</h2>
          <p class="section-copy">
            This console arms the GPS spoofing scenario. After arming, open the customer bus page
            and fetch a route that includes the same bus to render the spoofed fleet view and emit
            the anomaly logs.
          </p>

          <form
            class="detail-form"
            method="post"
            action="/api/simulations/gps-spoofing"
            data-console-form="gps-spoofing"
          >
            <div class="form-grid">
              <label>
                <span>Simulation Secret</span>
                <input type="text" name="simulation_secret" value="<%= simulationSecret %>" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Bus Number</span>
                <input type="text" name="bus_number" value="KA-01-FM-5520" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Route Name</span>
                <input type="text" name="route_name" value="Jayanagar - Airport" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Expected Location</span>
                <input type="text" name="expected_location" value="Jayanagar Depot" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Spoofed Location</span>
                <input type="text" name="spoofed_location" value="Airport Runway Access Road" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Anomaly Count</span>
                <input type="number" name="anomaly_count" min="1" max="50" value="5" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Jump Distance (km)</span>
                <input type="number" name="jump_distance_km" min="1" max="500" value="18" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Satellite Count</span>
                <input type="number" name="satellite_count" min="1" max="20" value="3" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Displayed Stop</span>
                <input type="text" name="displayed_stop" value="MG Road" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Schedule Delta (min)</span>
                <input type="number" name="schedule_delta_min" min="1" max="600" value="22" />
              </label>
              <label>
                <span>Anomaly Interval (ms)</span>
                <input type="number" name="anomaly_interval_ms" min="0" max="5000" value="50" />
              </label>
            </div>
            <label>
              <span>Operator Note</span>
              <textarea name="operator_note" rows="4">GPS spoofing drill for ghost-bus detection and route-integrity validation.</textarea>
            </label>
            <div class="form-actions">
              <button type="submit">Arm GPS Spoofing</button>
              <a class="ghost-link" href="/admin/dashboard">Back To Dashboard</a>
            </div>
          </form>
        </article>

        <article class="detail-card">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">Expected Events</p>
            <span class="status-pill success">Graylog Ready</span>
          </div>
          <h2>What Will Be Emitted</h2>
          <ul class="detail-list">
            <li>`message:gps_spoofing_armed` is emitted when the bus is staged.</li>
            <li>`message:gps_signal_anomaly` and `message:ghost_bus_projection` are emitted by the matching customer lookup.</li>
            <li>The customer fleet table will show the spoofed location and integrity state.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="chip-wrap">
            <span class="data-chip">message:gps_spoofing_armed</span>
            <span class="data-chip">message:gps_signal_anomaly</span>
            <span class="data-chip">message:ghost_bus_projection</span>
            <span class="data-chip">bus_number</span>
            <span class="data-chip">jump_distance_km</span>
          </div>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="detail-layout">
        <article class="detail-card detail-card-wide">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">Run Summary</p>
            <span class="status-pill neutral">API Response</span>
          </div>
          <div id="simulation-summary" class="result-empty">
            Arm the spoofing profile to view the accepted bus details, then run a matching customer
            fleet lookup to generate the anomaly evidence.
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="detail-card">
          <div class="card-topline">
            <p class="eyebrow">Raw API Body</p>
            <span class="status-pill neutral">JSON</span>
          </div>
          <pre id="console-response" class="response-pre">Run the console to inspect the response body.</pre>
        </article>
      </section>
    </main>
    <script src="/console.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
